   "subject": "Moderated mediation with latent variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi lavaaners,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I have modelled three latent variables in which one represents genetic data, the second brain volumetric information and the third severity of symptoms for a psychiatric disorder. During the analysis of this dataset I considered designing a mediation model in which symptom severity is regressed on the genetic latent either directly or via the brain volumetric latent. However, according to Kline (2015) mediation models assumes no interaction between the cause (genetic susceptibility) and the mediator (brain volume), which is likely not true in this case as the particular genes for the disorder susceptibility may be involved in the brain volume of those patients. Is it possible to specify a model such that the genetic latent interacts with the brain volume making this model a sort of a moderated mediation type of model? I could only find moderated mediation using categorical variables, not latent variables.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">The syntax for the model I have been testing is:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">total &lt;- &quot;\r\n\r\nvol =~  lh_parahippocampal_area + lh_entorhinal_area\r\n    + lh_transversetemporal_area + rh_temporalpole_area +lh_frontalpole_area\r\n    +rh_frontalpole_area\r\n\r\nsym =~ z_pos_2grp+ z_neg_2grp+ z_dis_2grp\r\n\r\ngen =~ BDNFord + EGFRord + IL3ord +FGFord #+ COMTord\r\n\r\nsym ~ c*gen\r\nvol ~ a*gen\r\nsym ~ b*vol\r\n\r\nab := a*b\r\n\r\ntotalaz := c+(a*b)\r\n&quot;\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Best,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">luis</p>\r\n<ol style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Kline RB. The Mediation Myth. Basic Appl. Soc. Psych. 2015;37(4):202-213. doi:10.1080/01973533.2015.1049349.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgbGF2YWFuZXJzLDxicj48YnI+SSBoYXZlIG1vZGVsbGVkIHRocmVlIGxhdGVudCB2YXJpYWJs\r\nZXMgaW4gd2hpY2ggb25lIHJlcHJlc2VudHMgZ2VuZXRpYyBkYXRhLCB0aGUgc2Vjb25kIGJyYWlu\r\nIHZvbHVtZXRyaWMgaW5mb3JtYXRpb24gYW5kIHRoZSB0aGlyZCBzZXZlcml0eSBvZiBzeW1wdG9t\r\ncyBmb3IgYSBwc3ljaGlhdHJpYyBkaXNvcmRlci4gRHVyaW5nIHRoZSBhbmFseXNpcyBvZiB0aGlz\r\nIGRhdGFzZXQgSSBjb25zaWRlcmVkIGRlc2lnbmluZyBhIG1lZGlhdGlvbiBtb2RlbCBpbiB3aGlj\r\naCBzeW1wdG9tIHNldmVyaXR5IGlzIHJlZ3Jlc3NlZCBvbiB0aGUgZ2VuZXRpYyBsYXRlbnQgZWl0\r\naGVyIGRpcmVjdGx5IG9yIHZpYSB0aGUgYnJhaW4gdm9sdW1ldHJpYyBsYXRlbnQuIEhvd2V2ZXIs\r\nIGFjY29yZGluZyB0byBLbGluZSAoMjAxNSkgbWVkaWF0aW9uIG1vZGVscyBhc3N1bWVzIG5vIGlu\r\ndGVyYWN0aW9uIGJldHdlZW4gdGhlIGNhdXNlIChnZW5ldGljIHN1c2NlcHRiaWxpdHkpIGFuZCB0\r\naGUgbWVkaWF0b3IgKGJyYWluIHZvbHVtZSksIHdoaWNoIGlzIGxpa2VseSBub3QgdHJ1ZSBpbiB0\r\naGlzIGNhc2UgYXMgdGhlIHBhcnRpY3VsYXIgZ2VuZXMgZm9yIHRoZSBkaXNvcmRlciBzdXNjZXB0\r\naWJpbGl0eSBtYXkgYmUgaW52b2x2ZWQgaW4gdGhlIGJyYWluIHZvbHVtZSBvZiB0aG9zZSBwYXRp\r\nZW50cy4gSXMgaXQgcG9zc2libGUgdG8gc3BlY2lmeSBhIG1vZGVsIHN1Y2ggdGhhdCB0aGUgZ2Vu\r\nZXRpYyBsYXRlbnQgaW50ZXJhY3RzIHdpdGggdGhlIGJyYWluIHZvbHVtZSBtYWtpbmcgdGhpcyBt\r\nb2RlbCBhIHNvcnQgb2YgYSBtb2RlcmF0ZWQgbWVkaWF0aW9uIHR5cGUgb2YgbW9kZWw/IEkgY291\r\nbGQgb25seSBmaW5kIG1vZGVyYXRlZCBtZWRpYXRpb24gdXNpbmcgY2F0ZWdvcmljYWwgdmFyaWFi\r\nbGVzLCBub3QgbGF0ZW50IHZhcmlhYmxlcy48YnI+PGJyPlRoZSBzeW50YXggZm9yIHRoZSBtb2Rl\r\nbCBJIGhhdmUgYmVlbiB0ZXN0aW5nIGlzOjxicj48YnI+YGBgPGJyPnRvdGFsICZsdDstICI8YnI+\r\nPGJyPnZvbCA9fsKgIGxoX3BhcmFoaXBwb2NhbXBhbF9hcmVhICsgbGhfZW50b3JoaW5hbF9hcmVh\r\nPGJyPsKgwqDCoCArIGxoX3RyYW5zdmVyc2V0ZW1wb3JhbF9hcmVhICsgcmhfdGVt