    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Dear Terrence and fellow lavaaners,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Sorry for bumping this discussion, but only now I could return to this problem.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">indProb</code> seems to be what I need to solve it, however I need further help on how to use it. For that, I will use a simpler model than the one originally posted. Please consider the model specification below:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">model7 &lt;- “\r\n    sch =~ pos_2grp+ neg_2grp+ dis_2grp\r\n    gen =~ BDNFord + EGFRord + IL3ord\r\n    cog =~  attention + verbal + workingm\r\n\r\n    sch ~ cprime * gen\r\n    sch ~ b * cog\r\n    sch ~ bprime * genXcog\r\n\r\n    cog ~ a * gen\r\n    cog ~~ genXcog\r\n    gen ~~ genXcog\r\n\r\n    bgen :=  b + bprime\r\n    indgen := bgen * a\r\n    indNgen := b * a\r\n    indDiff := indgen - indNgen\r\n ”\r\nfit7 &lt;- sem(model7, dataset, estimator = &quot;MLM&quot;)\r\nsummary(fit7)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Where sch is symptom severity measured in tests, cog is trivial cognitive testing (and the mediator) and gen is formed by ordinal variables (0=absence of risk allele, 1=heterozygous, 2=homozygous). The model I have in mind looks like the figure below, from the paper [^1]. On trying to run this specification, lavaan will complain that cog is not an observed variable and not run the analysis.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/l7HeYSimkgFPidG3vWnLJqpOI-PDtbzAj222T9rQl0io_Ga-V9yyP75twJVO0yIj1gki_Php=s0-d-e1-ft#https://i.stack.imgur.com/1Pnhj.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Now, if I try to follow your suggestion and run <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">indProd</code>:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">dataset&lt;-indProd(dataset, var1=c(&quot;BDNFord&quot;,&quot;EGFRord&quot;,&quot;IL3ord&quot;),\r\n                      var2=c(&quot;attention&quot;,&quot;verbal&quot;,&quot;workingm&quot;))\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">dataset</code> is now the dataset that includes BDNFord.attention, EGFRord.verbal, IL3ord.workingm. This is where I got stuck, how can I obtain a general product genXcog that allows me to use in this moderated mediation model?</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Thank you,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Luis</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">[^1]: Jeremy N.V Miles, Magdalena Kulesza, Brett Ewing, Regina A Shih, Joan S Tucker, Elizabeth J D’Amico, (2015) “Moderated<br>    mediation analysis: an illustration using the association of gender with delinquency and mental health”, Journal of Criminal<br>    Psychology, Vol. 5 Issue: 2, pp.99-123, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1108/JCP-02-2015-0010\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1108/JCP-02-2015-0010&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426626207000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iUn8ENslmAumliL_Z_-MG\">https://doi.org/10.1108/JCP-02-2015-0010</a></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:RGVhciBUZXJyZW5jZSBhbmQgZmVsbG93IGxhdmFhbmVycyw8YnI+PGJyPjxicj5Tb3JyeSBmb3Ig\r\nYnVtcGluZyB0aGlzIGRpc2N1c3Npb24sIGJ1dCBvbmx5IG5vdyBJIGNvdWxkIHJldHVybiB0byB0\r\naGlzIHByb2JsZW0uPGJyPjxicj48YnI+YGluZFByb2JgIHNlZW1zIHRvIGJlIHdoYXQgSSBuZWVk\r\nIHRvIHNvbHZlIGl0LCBob3dldmVyIEkgbmVlZCBmdXJ0aGVyIGhlbHAgb24gaG93IHRvIHVzZSBp\r\ndC4gRm9yIHRoYXQsIEkgd2lsbCB1c2UgYSBzaW1wbGVyIG1vZGVsIHRoYW4gdGhlIG9uZSBvcmln\r\naW5hbGx5IHBvc3RlZC4gUGxlYXNlIGNvbnNpZGVyIHRoZSBtb2RlbCBzcGVjaWZpY2F0aW9uIGJl\r\nbG93Ojxicj48YnI+YGBgPGJyPm1vZGVsNyAmbHQ7LSDigJw8YnI+wqDCoMKgIHNjaCA9fiBwb3Nf\r\nMmdycCsgbmVnXzJncnArIGRpc18yZ3JwPGJyPsKgwqDCoCBnZW4gPX4gQkRORm9yZCArIEVHRlJv\r\ncmQgKyBJTDNvcmQ8YnI+wqDCoMKgIGNvZyA9fsKgIGF0dGVudGlvbiArIHZlcmJhbCArIHdvcmtp\r\nbmdtPGJyPjxicj7CoMKgwqAgc2NoIH4gY3ByaW1lICogZ2VuPGJyPsKgwqDCoCBzY2ggfiBiICog\r\nY29nPGJyPsKgwqDCoCBzY2ggfiBicHJpbWUgKiBnZW5YY29nPGJyPjxicj7CoMKgwqAgY29nIH4g\r\nYSAqIGdlbjxicj7CoMKgwqAgY29nIH5+IGdlblhjb2c8YnI+wqDCoMKgIGdlbiB+fiBnZW5YY29n\r\nPGJyPjxicj7CoMKgwqAgYmdlbiA6PcKgIGIgKyBicHJpbWU8YnI+wqDCoMKgIGluZGdlbiA6PSBi\r\nZ2VuICogYTxicj7CoMKgwqAgaW5kTmdlbiA6PSBiICogYTxicj7CoMKgwqAgaW5kRGlmZiA6PSBp\r\nbmRnZW4gLSBpbmROZ2VuPGJyPuKAg+KAnTxicj5